# Copy to .env.local and fill in. None of these are required for the app to run.

# Per-trip password gates (see src/proxy.ts). Each trip route (/gb, /tuscany)
# prompts for its own password; a trip with no password serves 503 (fail
# closed). The home picker is not gated.
SITE_PASSWORD_GB=
SITE_PASSWORD_TUSCANY=

# Postgres. Leave unset: `pnpm dev` then starts a local database in .trips-db/.
# TRIPS_DATABASE_URL=

# Sign-in. `pnpm dev` with the local database sets a secret of its own, and
# writes each email as a JSON file to .trips-outbox/, where a local sign-up
# finds its code. A deployment needs TRIPS_AUTH_SECRET (a random 32-byte
# value, set once), RESEND_API_KEY with TRIPS_EMAIL_FROM for the emails, and
# Upstash Redis (KV_REST_API_URL, KV_REST_API_TOKEN) for the rate limits:
# without Redis it sends no email.
# TRIPS_AUTH_SECRET=
# TRIPS_EMAIL_FROM=

# Google Maps Embed API key — enables the inline route maps in the day view.
# Setup: Google Cloud console → enable "Maps Embed API" → create an API key →
# restrict it to your domain(s) (HTTP referrers) AND to the Maps Embed API.
# This value is public on purpose (it ships in the iframe URL), so the referrer
# restriction is what protects it. The Maps Embed API has no usage charge.
# Unset → maps are hidden and the app falls back to Google Maps deep-links.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_EMBED_API_KEY=
